From 5cd16cc2504966e4805c9d1ad2687926a378bdbf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Romeu Melur <romeumello@icloud.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 00:51:54 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] virtio/vsock: preserve half-close semantics in the unix proxy

When the host side of a unix socket proxy shuts down its write side,
recv() returns 0 and the proxy answered with a reset, so the guest
could never send its reply. Clients such as the Docker CLI half-close
every request stream (`docker exec`, piped stdin), and the response
was lost.

Translate that EOF into a send-only vsock shutdown, ordered after the
data already pushed, stop read polling and keep late credit updates
from restarting it, as the TSI stream proxy does since 3f76a106. Fatal
socket errors still reset the connection.

On macOS, set SO_NOSIGPIPE on accepted sockets too: the guest can now
keep writing after the host side is gone, and that write must fail
with EPIPE instead of killing the VMM with SIGPIPE.

Assisted-by: Claude Code: claude-opus-5-5
---
 .../src/virtio/vsock/unix_proxy/mod.rs        | 28 ++++++--
 .../src/virtio/vsock/unix_proxy/unix.rs       | 64 +++++++++++--------
 .../src/virtio/vsock/unix_proxy/windows.rs    | 24 ++++---
 3 files changed, 74 insertions(+), 42 deletions(-)

